node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
.DS_Store
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OpenWolf per-session runtime state. The useful files in .wolf/ (STATUS,
# cerebrum, buglog, memory) stay tracked; these two churn on every hook run.
.wolf/hooks/_session.json
.wolf/hooks/_precompact-snapshot.json
.wolf/token-ledger.json


# Local tooling scratch, not part of the project.
.gastown-ignore
__pycache__/

# Screenshot sources. The README serves the .webp beside them, converted with
# `cwebp -resize 900 0 -q 80 -m 6 shot.png -o shot.webp`. The PNGs are ~1-2MB
# each and would only ever be duplicates in the history.
docs/screenshots/*.png

# OpenWolf snapshots and pre-purge archives of .wolf/buglog.json. Runtime//backup
# state, never durable knowledge; the other OpenWolf repos ignore this too.
.wolf/backups/

# OpenWolf-generated files: never tracked.
#
# A colleague who clones this repo and installs OpenWolf gets every one of these
# regenerated locally, so tracking them only produces a diff on each upgrade and
# invites local edits that the next `openwolf update` silently strips. Do not
# "fix" a stale instruction in .wolf/OPENWOLF.md or .claude/rules/openwolf.md
# either - they are in the CLI's ALWAYS_OVERWRITE list. Project-specific
# corrections belong in CLAUDE.md, which OpenWolf does not manage.
#
# Still tracked, because `openwolf update` preserves them as user data (see
# USER_DATA_FILES in the CLI's update.js): .wolf/cerebrum.md, .wolf/STATUS.md,
# .wolf/config.json, and .wolf/buglog.json where a repo keeps it.
#
# Set up a fresh clone with:  openwolf init --agent claude
#   (--agent claude matters: a bare init also writes .codex/ + AGENTS.md)
.wolf/OPENWOLF.md
.wolf/reframe-frameworks.md
.wolf/identity.md
.wolf/hooks/
.wolf/cron-manifest.json
.wolf/cron-state.json
.wolf/suggestions.json
.wolf/_scan-state.json
.wolf/anatomy.md
.wolf/anatomy-index.json
.wolf/memory.md
.claude/rules/openwolf.md
.claude/settings.json
.claude/commands/designqc.md
.claude/commands/reframe.md
.claude/commands/security-audit.md
.claude/skills/designqc/
.claude/skills/reframe/
.codex/
.opencode/
AGENTS.md
